    ":question/id": "f043b7ca-be08-556b-94ec-1d757642bb0f",
    ":question/problem": "$\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})=$",
    ":question/worked-solution": "Recall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u-v)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for sine with $u=x$ and $v=\\frac{\\pi }{4},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x).\\end{aligned}\n$$"
  },
