    ":question/problem": "Express $\\operatorname{sin}(x-\\frac{7\\pi }{4})$ in terms of $\\operatorname{sin}x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}x.$\n\n$\\operatorname{sin}(x-\\frac{7\\pi }{4})=$\n{{field-1}}$\\operatorname{sin}x\\,+$\n{{field-2}}$\\operatorname{cos}x$",
    ":question/worked-solution": "Recall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}(u-v)=\\operatorname{sin}u\\operatorname{cos}v-\\operatorname{cos}u\\operatorname{sin}v\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for sine with $u=x$ and $v=\\frac{7\\pi }{4},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}(x-\\frac{7\\pi }{4}) & =\\operatorname{sin}x\\operatorname{cos}\\left(\\frac{7\\pi }{4}\\right)-\\operatorname{cos}x\\operatorname{sin}\\left(\\frac{7\\pi }{4}\\right) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}x\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-\\operatorname{cos}x\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}x}{2}+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}x}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,\\operatorname{sin}x+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,\\operatorname{cos}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
  },
